{
  "title": "continues_on_failure is defined inconsistently across types.rs, \
step metadata, and job outcomes",
  "description": "There are two parallel definitions of which pipeline steps \
fail soft, and they disagree. \
ramekin_core::types::PipelineStep::continues_on_failure() says EnrichAutoTag \
and ApplyAutoTags continue on failure. But the step structs' own metadata() — \
which is what the server runner and core executor actually consult — says \
continues_on_failure: false for ALL enrich steps (enrich_normalize_title, \
enrich_generate_description, and enrich_auto_tag, whose comment 'Errors should \
stop the pipeline' directly contradicts types.rs); only the server's \
ApplyAutoTagsStep is true. The practical consequence: when any AI enrichment \
fails (invalid or missing OPENROUTER_API_KEY, provider flake), the recipe is \
saved but the whole job is marked FAILED at the enrich step, even though \
enrich steps carefully set next_step on failure as if they expected to fail \
soft. Commit 8c9b6da23 (#526) says 'Mark ingest failed when a non-continuing \
post-save apply step fails', so some of this is deliberate, but agents keep \
misreading the design (a since-removed ios.yml comment claimed enrich steps \
are continues_on_failure). Decide the intended semantics — should a post-save \
enrichment failure fail the job, or complete it with per-step failures \
surfaced (status.rs already renders failed steps inside completed jobs) — then \
make types.rs, the step metadata, and the comments agree, and delete whichever \
definition is redundant. Affects how import failures render in both the web \
scrape-status UI and the iOS import UI; behavior should stay consistent for \
both clients.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "server",
    "pipeline",
